cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Phantom Vision Lab â€” a computational instrument for perturbing an image-analysis pipeline and measuring how its output changes"
message: "If you use this software, read the 'What this is not' section of the README first. It is classical computer vision, not a neural network, and it measures no consciousness."
type: software
abstract: >-
  A research instrument that generates 16 deterministic structured-light pattern
  types from a seed, runs each through a fixed classical computer-vision analysis
  pipeline twice â€” once unmodified and once with 11 computational parameters
  perturbed â€” and reports how much the analysis output changed. Determinism is
  byte-identical across fresh interpreter processes. The software loads no neural
  network, measures no subjective experience, and reproduces no biological altered
  state; "perception" throughout is a metaphor for output-structure analysis. The
  perception divergence score has no validated interpretation scale and no
  threshold in this software has been empirically established. Ships with a
  documented account of three false claims found in the previous documentation.
authors:
  - name: "Phantom Vision Lab contributors"
